      // ~110 px and rise ~30 px; grown and turned, a piece ends ~65 px wide, so the burst covers cx +-145 and
      // cy-175 .. cy+120), framing the shape coming in
      // instead of covering its face or the message. Wide screens with a big hole and the message off to the
      // side: from the top edge of the hole. Elsewhere (tall screens, where the message pill sits right above
      // the hole, and short landscape phones): from beside the hole, low enough that no piece reaches the pill
      // and far enough out that none ends on the shape's face; on the side away from the tile where the whole
      // burst fits, else on the left. (A piece past the stage's right or bottom edge would make the stage
      // scrollable for a moment; past the left edge it is simply cut off, as a stage never scrolls left.)
      // Portrait phones are too narrow for that (a third of the burst would be off the screen): there it bursts
      // from beside the tile that was tapped - 70 px to the side with more room, so the shape flies clear of it;
      // level with the tile, and at least 150 px (175 where there is room) under the face in the hole. (A short
      // screen with no such room under the face keeps the burst beside the hole.)
